# {{PRODUCT}} Android agent instructions

Read `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; it is the authoritative safety contract.

- Graph-backed discovery (`task-context` / `graph`); search never anchors initial discovery. Never inspect `.agents/scripts/**` during normal app work.
- Clarify ambiguity in chat before planning. Approved plan required for mutations; after approval, execute phases autonomously. Follow-ups within active scope execute immediately: never generate redundant plan artifacts or stall for nonexistent UI buttons (record refinements via `task plan-note`).
- Match the developer's conversation language using the canonical cards from `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` (including the 3-section **Mobile Verification Walkthrough**). In RTL languages, start every line/option with a word in that language and wrap symbols, paths, and English terms in `` `backticks` ``.
- 6-tier policy (`T0_TRIVIAL` to `T5_CRITICAL`) governs gates, reviewers, and device checks. Never self-certify HIGH/CRITICAL reviews with `record_review.py --verdict PASS`. Never poll background work (Zero-Polling invariant). On Antigravity, delegate multi-file read sweeps to `harness-scout-agent` and `T0–T3` non-sensitive implementation/Gradle slices to a single `harness-worker-agent` (`delegate-plan --json`), reviewing `git diff` on return.
- Clarify and translate durable rules into English before `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<english-note>"`; always follow `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md`.

## Canonical Command Catalog

| Step | Command |
|---|---|
| Discovery | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` / `graph --feature <name> --json` |
| Status / Gates | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next` / `preflight` / `test` |
| Reviews | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` -> `review finalize --task <id>` |
| Device / Verify | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` -> `device install-start` -> `verify --task-id <id>` |

